From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:04:59 -0700
Subject: [navigation] Match MHTML MIME types case-insensitively in the browser

Per RFC 2045 Section 5.1, media types and subtypes are case-insensitive.
However, browser process MHTML classification in
NavigationRequest::IsMhtmlMimeType(), download_utils::MustDownload(),
and IntentHandler.isMhtmlMimeType() used exact, case-sensitive string
equality for "multipart/related" and "message/rfc822". Meanwhile,
non-HTTP loaders like Android's ContentURLLoader forwarded unnormalized
MIME types from ContentProvider.getType().

Bug: 574381704
Change-Id: I5aa204c725c075d36ee31f7bafebda89b5f4fe58
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8620417
Reviewed-by: Ted Choc <tedchoc@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Nasko Oskov <nasko@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725439}

